16. NO `cd` / CURRENT DIRECTORY YET

Do not add:

- cd
- pwd
- shell working-directory state
- per-Terminal current directory
- canonical working-directory state

`ls` and `cat` operate on explicit absolute paths in this slice.

A real working-directory concept may later belong to a concrete operating
context when remote shells exist.

Do not solve that future problem here.


17. LOCAL FILESYSTEM ONLY

This milestone applies only to:

player.localDevice

Do not attach a filesystem to every existing NetworkHost.

Do not add remote filesystem access.

Do not make successful DeviceAccess imply filesystem access.

The later remote operating-context / foreign Device milestones will establish
the correct boundary first.

Specifically:

DeviceAccess ≠ remote filesystem access.


18. DO NOT CHANGE PROCESS EXECUTION

Filesystem reads are immediate local observations.

Do not make `ls` or `cat` Processes.

Do not:

- consume CPU work
- reserve RAM
- create Process history
- change Process scheduling
- change executorDeviceId

Existing Process behavior remains unchanged.


19. DO NOT CREATE FILESYSTEM GAMEPLAY ARTIFACTS YET

This slice establishes the storage surface.

It does not yet establish artifact production.

Do not generate files because the player:

- scans
- analyzes
- attacks
- gains DeviceAccess
- runs commands
- opens applications

Do not create fake logs.

Later concrete gameplay can mutate filesystem state when represented events
actually justify artifacts.


